00\u2500\nMarket-implied horizon: reverse DCF shows the price underwriting ~19-21%\ngrowth through 2033 (\u2248 7+ years of hyper-growth) \u2014 i.e., the market is\npaying today for a decade-long runway.\nMy horizon: 3-5 years. Spread = My horizon (3-5y) - Market horizon (~10y)\n= NEGATIVE (-5 years).\nNo arbitrage opportunity for a value-timing framework; the market's\nembedded expectations EXCEED what we can support. Buying here means funding\nthe market's optimism, not exploiting its pessimism.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 5-1. Conviction score (/15):\n1. Business quality: 3/3 (wide moat, net cash, ROIC 26%, 63% GM)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 0/3 (IV $156 vs price $224 = -44% MoS)\n3. Macro alignment: 1/3 (headwind: 4.7% 10Y, duration risk)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3/3 (KPIs: revenue growth, GAAP/non-GAAP OI margins,\n   units, retention \u2014 all reported quarterly)\n5. Execution traceability: 3/3 (guided and raised twice; margins landing)\nTOTAL: 10/15 \u2192 HIGH (business/thesis conviction) but the valuation pillar\nis zero, which caps any position at 0%.\nStep 5-2. Conviction decay: -1 per 6 months without confirming evidence \u2192\ninitiate at 10/15, decays toward 9.\nStep 5-3. Sizing: With MoS < 0%, framework sizing = 0% for new money.\nMax weight if a position were somehow justifie