B: S&P Global consensus. [Estimate \u2014 stockanalysis.com, 2026-07-27]\n\u2022 FY2028+ growth: my assumption; decelerating from 15% to 8.5% because growth beyond 2027 is not established. [Assumption]\n\u2022 Adj FCF margins: my assumption; improvement from TTM 19.1% toward 23.5% terminal, supported by consensus non-GAAP operating margin of ~19.5% for 2026. [Estimate \u2014 S&P Global implied]\n\u2022 Terminal growth: 3.5%, below nominal GDP. [Assumption]\n\nDiscounting (WACC 9.5%, end-of-year):\nPV of explicit FCF: $2.59B [Arithmetic]\nTerminal value: $0.746B \u00d7 1.035 / (0.095 - 0.035) = $12.87B [Arithmetic]\nPV of terminal value: $5.19B [Arithmetic]\nEnterprise value: $7.78B [Arithmetic]\nNet cash: $0.069B [Arithmetic]\nEquity value: $7.85B [Arithmetic]\nDiluted shares: 36.33M (FY2025 weighted diluted). [Actual]\nBase intrinsic value per share: ~$216 [Estimate]\n\nMultiples cross-check:\n\u2022 2026E non-GAAP EPS $6.90 (S&P Global consensus). [Estimate]\n\u2022 2026E P/E at $216: 31.3x. [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 2027E EPS $8.43 \u2192 25.6x. [Arithmetic]\n\u2022 EV/2026E revenue: $7.78B / $1.122B = 6.9x. [Arithmetic]\nA fair 2026E P/E of 30\u201333x gives $207\u2013228; my DCF sits inside that range. Trailing P/E of 44.8x is rich but distorted by one-time FY2024 tax benefit. [Estimate]\n\nReverse DCF:\nAt $224.4, the market is pricing either ~+2 percentage points of revenue growth per year versus my base case, or a terminal adjusted FCF margin 100\u2013150bps above my base case, or a 0.5\u20131.0 point lower WACC. That is achievable only if AI premium adoption holds. [Assumption/Estimate]\n\nSensitivity of base IV per share (WACC / terminal growth):\n\u2022 WACC 8.5%, g 3.5%: ~$262 [Estimate]\n\u2022 WACC 9.0%, g 3.5%: ~$236 [Estimate]\n\u2022 WACC 9.5%, g 3.5%: ~$216 [Estimate]\n\u2022 WACC 10.0%, g 3.5%: ~$198 [Estimate]\n\u2022 WACC 9.5%, g 3.0%: ~$199 [Estimate]\n\u2022 WACC 9.5%, g 4.0%: ~$235 [Estimate]\n\nTornado top-3 variables:\n1. Revenue growth after 2027.\n2. Terminal adjusted FCF margin.\n3. WACC / long-term rates.\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n\u2022 Competitive response: If Realm-X succeeds, Yardi and Entrata will replicate AI features and bundle them into existing contracts, pressuring ARPU. Counter-move impact: -2. [Estimate]\n\u2022 Reflexivity: High stock price supports talent recruiting via SBC and gives M&A currency. Current price is 22% below the 52-week high, so positive reflexivity has weakened but not reversed. [Estimate]\n\u2022 Customer evolution: AI adoption is spreading from early adopters to mainstream; 44% of property managers now use AI vs 29% last year. As penetration matures, unit growth will slow but switching costs rise. [Estimate \u2014 AppFolio/NAA Benchmark Report]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\nScenario probabilities: Bear 25%, Base 50%, Bull 25%. Base is the highest probability. [Assumption]\n\n\u2022 Bear ($110/share): Revenue fade to 4% growth, terminal adjusted FCF margin 18%, WACC 10%, terminal growth 3%. Legal opening of platform and AI commoditization. Probability: 25%. [Estimate]\n\u2022 Base ($216/share): Company hits FY2026 guidance and FY2027