ding (3 sentences):\nAppFolio sells cloud property-management software (accounting, leasing,\nmaintenance, screening, payments, owner portals) to ~22,751 professional\nproperty managers covering 9.6M units [Actual, Q2 2026 call]. It monetizes a\ncore subscription plus premium AI-native tiers (RealmX, AI workflows) and\nvalue-added services, riding an industry shift toward tech-stack\nconsolidation (45% of PMs planning consolidation [Actual, AppFolio\nbenchmark]). Growth is unit-driven (~20% YoY) with high retention and\nexpanding margins.\nUnderstandability: HIGH.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat score (7 types, 0-3 each):\n- Intangible assets (brand/patents): 1\n- Switching costs: 3  (mission-critical operational system; migration from\n  6-14 disconnected systems cited by customers [Actual, call])\n- Network effects: 2  (data pooled across 9.6M units improves AI outcomes)\n- Cost advantage: 2  (SaaS scale economics)\n- Economies of scale: 2 (22.7k customers; R&D leverage)\n- Regulatory barriers: 1 (screening/background-check is regulated but not a\n  durable entry barrier; litigation here is an overhang, not a moat)\n- Data moat: 2 (9.6M units; AI training set; widening)\nTOTAL: 13/21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT (lower end).\nMoat direction: WIDENING \u2014 units +, consolidation tailwind, AI data flywheel,\npremium attach growth; partially offset by Yardi/Entrata counter-investment.\nConviction in \"wide\": MEDIUM-HIGH.\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch classification: FAST GROWER, transitioning to STALWART\n(2026 growth ~18% vs 25% 5-yr CAGR [pack S7]). Checkpoints: growth rate\nstill >15% (PASS, Q2 +19.3% [pack]); no debt (PASS, net cash); insider\nownership 4.54% [pack S9] \u2014 acceptable, not a red flag; SBC at 7.5% of\nrevenue is the main \"growth financed by dilution\" concern (see 2.5).\n\nStep 2-4. Financial strength scorecard (FY2025 [Filed] unless noted):\n- Revenue growth: 3-yr CAGR 38.4% [Arithmetic: (0.951/0.359)^(1/3)-1];\n  5-yr CAGR 25.1% [pack S7]; last-4Q growth 19-22% [pack S4]\n- Operating margin: FY25 16.1% [Arithmetic]; Q2-26 18.8% [Actual, call];\n  3-yr avg ~11% [Arithmetic]\n- EPS growth: distorted by one-time items (2024 NI $0.204B > OI $0.136B =>\n  deferred-tax benefit; 2020 similar). Normalized EPS growing ~15% [Estimate]\n- ROE FY25: 0.141/((0.297+0.543)/2) = 33.6% [Arithmetic]; ROIC ~26%\n  [Estimate: NOPAT 0.122 / (equity 0.543 + leases 0.038 - cash 0.107) = 0.474]\n- FCF margin FY25: 25.1% reported [Arithmetic: 0.239/0.951]; owner-earnings\n  margin ~17.7% [Arithmetic: (0.242-0.003-0.071)/0.951]\n- FCF conversion: OCF/NI = 1.72x [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: NET CASH +$0.069B (cash 0.107 - leases 0.038; no other debt in\n  FY25 [pack S6/S6B]); vendor total-debt cross-check 0.038 confirms [pack S2]\n- Interest coverage: n/a (no debt)\nVERDICT: EXCELLENT.\n\nStep 2-5. Capital allocation scorecard (0-3 each, /15):\n1. Buyback efficiency: 1 (share count fell 36.78M\u219235.42M ~ -3.7% over 2024-26\n   [pack], but buybacks executed at 40-50x earnings \u2014 offsetting SBC at high\n   prices is only mildly accretive)\n2. M&A track record: 1 (small tuck-ins only; no data on returns [Unconfirmed])\n3. Capex efficiency: 3 (capex 0.3% of revenue; incremental ROIC very high)\n4. Rationality of mix: 2 (reinvest in AI/R&D > buyback; no dividend; coherent)\n5. Guidance accuracy: 3 (raised FY26 guidance twice: $1.11-1.125B \u2192 $1.117-\n   1.127B; consistently beats)\nTOTAL: 10/15. Insider bonus: 0 (4.54% ownership; no 6-mo net-buy evidence in\npack). NET: 10/15 \u2014 GOOD.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANG