                                                    5.517\n\u00f7 35.417M shares [pack S2]                                          = $155.8/sh\nBASE-CASE IV \u2248 $156/share  (50% CI $130-185; 80% CI $105-220)\n\nSENSITIVITY (Tornado \u2014 top 3 variables drive Thesis KPIs):\n(a) WACC: 8.5%\u2192$166 | 9.2%\u2192$156 | 10.0%\u2192~$143  [Assumption range]\n(b) Terminal GAAP OI: 22%\u2192~$140 | 25%\u2192$156 | 28%\u2192~$168\n(c) Growth path: fast-fade (12\u21925% by 2029)\u2192~$130 | base\u2192$156 |\n    slow-fade (18% to 2028)\u2192~$172\n(d) Tax: 12%\u2192~$163 | 15%\u2192$156 | 20%\u2192$147\n\nREVERSE DCF (what the price implies): EV 7.879B (7.948 - 0.107 + 0.038).\nMinus PV explicit FCFF 1.851 \u21d2 implied PV(TV) 6.03B \u21d2 TV 11.7B \u21d2\nFCFF_t 0.724 \u21d2 NOPAT_t 0.826 \u21d2 OI_2033 ~0.97 \u21d2 at 25% GAAP margin,\nrevenue_2033 \u2248 $3.9B \u21d2 2026-33 CAGR \u2248 19-20%. The market is pricing\n~19-21% annual growth for SEVEN consecutive years with margin expansion \u2014\nabove the top of our plausible range. VERDICT: the price = our most\naggressive bull case (SECTION 4).\n\nMULTIPLES CROSS-CHECK (at $224.40):\n- EV/S 2026E: 7.0x (7.879/1.122)\n- P/E TTM GAAP: 50.3x (224.40/4.46) | 2027E GAAP: ~39x\n- Non-GAAP P/E 2027E: ~27x (adds back SBC \u2014 framework treats SBC as a real\n  cost, so we do NOT anchor here; shown for transparency)\n- EV/EBITDA 2026E GAAP: ~34x | P/FCF owner-earnings TTM: ~42x\n- PEG (GAAP, ~17% growth): ~2.8\nConclusion: no multiple-based case supports $224 on a cash basis; the\nnon-GAAP multiple only \"works\" if SBC is ignored.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n3.5-1. Competitive response: if APPF keeps winning share (24% non-GAAP OI\ngrowth, 9.6M units), Yardi (larger, private, deep pockets) and Entrata will\nrespond on price/AI; Beagle Labs' antitrust theory (denying third-party\naccess) is exactly the vector competitors will press (-2 on pricing power\n2-3 years out). Response: model's fade path already embeds this; it does NOT\nembed a price war (downside case = Bear).\n3.5-2. Reflexivity: positive loop is live (AI narrative \u2192 95.7% institutional\nownership \u2192 currency for talent via SBC \u2192 product \u2192 growth). Negative loop\nwould trigger if the multiple breaks (talent/SBC economics reverse).\nCurrently positive, but this is what makes a de-rating non-linear.\n3.5-3. Customer evolution: early adopters \u2192 mainstream (22,751 customers;\nPMs consolidating from 6-14 systems [Actual call]) \u2192 late adopters will be\nprice-sensitive and slower; expect LTV/CAC to degrade and churn to rise as\npenetration passes ~50% of the SMB-to-mid multifamily TAM (est. ~40-50% now\n[Assumption]). This supports a growth fade \u2014 not an acceleration.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4. SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nBAYESIAN UPDATE: Prior P(>15% growth to 2029) \u2248 50% (base rate, 1.5-1).\nEvidence at T0: guidance raised twice, units + to 9.6M, non-GAAP OI 27.1%,\nretention \"strong\" [Actual call]. Likelihood ratio \u2248 1.25 [Assumption].\nPosterior \u2248 55-60%. Applied to scenario weights below.\n\nScenario set (sums to 100%):\n- BEAR 25% \u2014 Growth cliff: Yardi/AI price war + legal overhang \u2192 growth\n  fades to 5% by 2029, GAAP OI stalls at 22%, WACC 10%, tax 18%:\n  IV \u2248 $110/sh (range $95-125)\n- BASE 50% \u2014 Guidance-anchored fade: growth 18\u21925% by 2033, GAAP OI \u2192 25%,\n  WACC 9.2%, tax 15%: IV \u2248 $156/sh (range $130-185)\n- BULL 25% \u2014 AI share-gain: 18% growth sustained to 2028 then 8% fade,\n  GAAP OI \u2192 28%, WACC 8.5%, tax 15%: IV \u2248 $222/sh (range $195-240)\n\nExpected value = 0.25\u00d7110 + 0.50\u00d7156 + 0.25\u00d7222 = $161/sh\nExpected price at T0 vs $224.40 \u2192 expected downside \u2248 -28% to -39%\n(vs E[V] and base respectively).\nMargin of safety: (156-224)/156 = -43.6% vs base \u2192 NONE (violates the\n>30%-MoS \"Strong\" bar massively on the wrong side).\n50% CI $130-185 does NOT contain the market price; 80% CI $105-220 barely\ntouches it. Only the BULL case reaches the market price \u2014 and even it\nrequires a sub-9% discount rate.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4.5. HORIZON ARBITRAGE\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nMarket-implied horizon: reverse DCF shows the price underwriting ~19-21%\ngrowth through 2033 (\u2248 7+ years of hyper-growth) \u2014 i.e., the market is\npaying today for a decade-long runway.\nMy horizon: 3-5 years. Spread = My horizon (3-5y) - Market horizon (~10y)\n= NEGATIVE (-5 years).\nNo arbitrage opportunity for a value-timing framework; the market's\nembedded expectations EXCEED what we can support. Buying here means funding\nthe market's optimism, not exploiting its pessimism.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 5. CONVICTION & POSITIONING\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\nStep 5-1. Conviction score (/15):\n1. Business quality: 3/3 (wide moat, net cash, ROIC 26%, 63% GM)\n2. Valuation attractiveness: 0/3 (IV $156 vs price $224 = -44% MoS)\n3. Macro alignment: 1/3 (headwind: 4.7% 10Y, duration risk)\n4. Thesis clarity: 3/3 (KPIs: revenue growth, GAAP/non-GAAP OI margins,\n   units, retention \u2014 all reported quarterly)\n5. Execution traceability: 3/3 (guided and raised twice; margins landing)\nTOTAL: 10/15 \u2192 HIGH (business/thesis conviction) but the valuation pillar\nis zero, which caps any position at 0%.\nStep 5-2. Conviction decay: -1 per 6 months without confirming evidence \u2192\ninitiate at 10/15, decays toward 9.\nStep 5-3. Sizing: With Mo