; \u226512% FY28 | Quarterly [Actual] |\n| GAAP EBIT margin | \u226518% FY26; \u226520% FY27; \u226522% FY28 | Quarterly |\n| Non-GAAP margin | Within 26.5-28.0% guide | Quarterly |\n| SBC / revenue | \u22648% (FY25 = 7.5%) | Annual |\n| Units on platform | Continue 8-12% growth | Quarterly |\n| Adjusted FCF margin | \u226517% of revenue (post-SBC) | Annual |\n| 10Y Treasury | \u22644.75% to hold macro neutral | Monthly |\n\nPre-Mortem (3 failure paths, early warnings):\n1. **AI Feature Parity War** \u2192 Yardi/Entrata launch equivalent AI at lower price \u2192 early sign: NRR < 100%, premium-tier attach stalls.\n2. **Legal/Regulatory Leakage** \u2192 Beagle Labs wins forced API access; damages > $100-200M; FTC follow-on \u2192 early sign: adverse summary-judgment rulings, settlement reserve building.\n3. **Demand Freeze (Stagflation)** \u2192 vacancies rise > prior cycle, tech spend frozen \u2192 early sign: customer count declines, revenue/unit flat for 2 quarters.\n\nEvents that force re-evaluation: guidance withdrawal; margin < 15% GAAP for 2 quarters; acquisition > $1B; change in CEO; 10Y > 5.25%.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS (Layer 9)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nStep 9-1: Short Thesis\n1. At $224, the market pays ~50x trailing GAAP and ~7x forward revenue for a vertical SaaS whose core unit penetration is already ~40-48% of its niche; the \"TAM\" narrative ignores that share gains slow at scale.\n2. GAAP vs non-GAAP gap is ~8pts \u2014 driven by 7.5% SBC; real FCF after SBC is $0.17-0.19B, not $0.27B. True valuation is >40x adjusted FCF.\n3. Yardi (private, much larger) and Entrata will outspend AppFolio on AI; feature gaps close within 2-4 quarters; price competition in mid-market follows.\n4. End-market is late-cycle: rising vacancies and 86% of managers already in defense mode pressure software budgets; APPF is not immune despite recurring SaaS.\n5. Legal overhang: Beagle Labs antitrust (platform access) and data-breach class actions create multi-year cost/uncertainty; FTC settlement is done but signals regulatory attention to screening business.\n6. Rate regime is hostile: 10Y at 4.71%, hawkish hold, hike odds ~1/3; long-duration assets compress first.\n7. Insider ownership 4.54% and institutional ownership 95.7% \u2014 no \"insider conviction\" signal; passive flows can reverse.\n\nStep 9-2: Logic Combat\nLong logic score: 9/10 (verified growth, actual margin expansion, raised guide, wide moat, net cash).\nShort logic score: 7.5/10 (valuation-driven, relies on competition/pricing parity that has not yet appeared; lacks a near-term fundamental catalyst).\n**Gap = 1.5 < 2 \u2192 conviction downgrade applied (already reflected: 9.5/15).**\n\nStep 9-3: Adversarial Data Points\nFTC settlement [Actual], Beagle Labs active suits [Estimate], data-breach notices [Estimate] \u2014 all sourced; no Hindenburg-style public short report surfaced in retrieval.\n\nStep 9-4: Killed Arguments\n- \"SaaS always deserves 40x+\": killed by 2021-22 multiple compressions in higher-rate regimes.\n- \"9.6M units = massive remaining runway\": partially killed \u2014 core professional-managed-unit penetration likely 40-48% [Estimate]; future growth must come from pricing/cross-sell, which is harder.\n- \"AI moat is unassailable\": killed \u2014 Yardi/Entrata have comparable data scale and deeper pockets; AI differentiation window is 2-3 years, not permanent.\n- \"FCF $0.27B is clean\": killed \u2014 pack's filed capex excludes capitalized software; vendor shows a 2.09x higher figure; SBC is a real expense.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 10. AUDIT RESULTS (Layer 8)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nA. Methodology: PASS \u2014 Engine 1 appropriate; no DCF-only conclusions (multiples + reverse DCF cross-checks); no TAM narrative-only (quantified penetration cap); macro not ignored.\nB. Valuation: PASS \u2014 WACC derived explicitly; terminal \u2264 nominal GDP; sensitivity matrix shown; reverse DCF checked; time-points not mixed (all forecasts from FY26E base).\nC. Bias: PASS with one flag \u2014 I initially anchored on the vendor's clean FCF figure; corrected by filing-level SBC/capex treatment. Overconfidence check: IV range $109-298; 80% CI stated.\nD. Consistency: PASS \u2014 market cap 7.948 / 35.417M shares = $224.4 \u2713; FY26 growth 18.0% consistent with $1.122B guide \u2713.\nE. Narrative: PASS \u2014 no unsupported \"platform premium\" or \"large long-term potential\" language; every driver tagged.\nF. Red Team: PASS \u2014 short thesis written from same data; gap 1.5; conviction downgraded.\nG. Data Integrity: PARTIAL \u2014 items not retrievable: DXY, credit spreads, GDP, options positioning, insider cluster trades, R&D split, effective-tax reconciliation, FY25 ST/LT investments. All are declared [Unconfirmed], not imputed. Pack's capex and vendor capex conflict (2.09x) \u2014 I used filed for history and 3% of revenue as conservative forecast. Pack's SBC vendor scalar is period-unreliable \u2014 I used filed series. Macrotrends TTM SBC $0.179B [Estimate] conflicts with the filed annual $0.071B; I did NOT adopt it (flagged; likely inconsistent basis).\nOverall: **PASS \u2014 no recalculation required; but model confidence is MODERATE, not high, due to Tiers 4-5 inputs (post-guided-period growth, margins, legal costs).**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 11. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY (Layer 7.4)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nDate: 2026-08-24 | T0: $224.40 | Expected IV: $199 | Base IV: $195 | MoS: -11%\nKey assumptions logged: WACC 8.6%; terminal growth 3.5%; 2031 GAAP EBIT margin 25%; 2031 revenue $2.07B; SBC \u22487.3-7.5% of revenue; tax 12%; shares 35.8M.\nRed-team concerns: (1) valuation embeds 32% margins; (2) Yardi AI parity; (3) late-cycle end-market; (4) legal overhang; (5) rates >4.75%.\nDi